model FileSystem

-- Whole-part filesystem model, built specifically to exercise the
-- KK-ModelValidator plugin's two "Miscellaneous" config-file toggles
-- documented in Usage.pdf's "Configuration using a property file" section:
--
--   aggregationcyclefreeness = on|off  (default on)
--     "no cycles are allowed inside of aggregations and compositions"
--   forbiddensharing = on|off          (default on)
--     "objects participating in a composition can[not] be member of more
--      than one composition"
--
-- Both toggles are model-level solver settings, not OCL; they live entirely
-- in the .properties files (FileSystem_default.properties /
-- FileSystem_off.properties), not in this .use file.
--
-- IMPORTANT MODELING NOTE, discovered by reading the installed plugin's own
-- source (org.tzi.kodkod.model.impl.Association.cycleFreenessDefinitions,
-- org.tzi.kodkod.model.impl.Class.forbiddingSharingDefinition) and then
-- confirming empirically:
--   - A cycle formed by a SINGLE aggregation/composition association
--     applied to itself (e.g. a lone self-referential Folder-contains-
--     Folder association) is compiled into an UNCONDITIONAL Kodkod
--     constraint that ignores the aggregationcyclefreeness toggle
--     entirely -- such a cycle is TRIVIALLY_UNSATISFIABLE whether the
--     toggle is on or off. This was our first design attempt; it produced
--     identical UNSATISFIABLE results in both configs (a real, confirmed
--     limitation of this plugin build -- see this example's README-style
--     notes / the task report's "warnings" section).
--   - Sharing of the same object between two DIFFERENT composition
--     associations that both declare the EXACT SAME class at their part
--     end is likewise an unconditional Kodkod constraint, ignoring the
--     forbiddensharing toggle.
--   - The toggles DO have an observable, confirmed effect for the two
--     structural shapes modeled below instead: a cycle that only closes
--     across TWO DIFFERENT associations (PrimaryContains/AltContains,
--     matching the baseline USE distribution's own
--     examples/Documentation/AggregationsAndCompositions/nocycle06.use
--     fixture), and sharing that only becomes visible once inheritance is
--     involved (FolderHasFile's part end is File; ArchiveHasMedia's part
--     end is the subclass MediaFile -- the plugin's per-class Kodkod check
--     matches part-end classes by exact equality, not by subtype, so
--     neither association alone triggers its unconditional constraint,
--     while USE core's own general checkStructure() graph walk -- which IS
--     gated by the config toggle -- still recognizes a single MediaFile
--     object doubly owned once the object diagram is reconstructed).

class Folder
attributes
  name : String
end

class File
attributes
  name : String
  size : Integer
end

class MediaFile < File
attributes
  codec : String
end

class Archive
attributes
  name : String
end

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Two INDEPENDENT self-referential composition hierarchies on Folder.
-- Neither one is cyclic by itself; forcing a link in each that together
-- close a 2-hop cycle ACROSS both associations is exactly the shape
-- aggregationcyclefreeness is meant to forbid, and (per the note above) is
-- the shape whose Kodkod-level enforcement is actually gated by the
-- toggle in this plugin build.
composition PrimaryContains between
  Folder [0..1] role primaryParent
  Folder [0..*] role primarySubfolders
end

composition AltContains between
  Folder [0..1] role altParent
  Folder [0..*] role altSubfolders
end

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Two DIFFERENT composition associations whose part-end classes are File
-- and its subclass MediaFile respectively. A concrete MediaFile object can
-- be forced into both (it IS a File), which is exactly the whole-object
-- "member of more than one composition" case forbiddensharing is meant to
-- forbid.
composition FolderHasFile between
  Folder [0..1] role ownerFolder
  File   [0..*] role files
end

composition ArchiveHasMedia between
  Archive   [0..1] role ownerArchive
  MediaFile [0..*] role archivedMedia
end

------------------------------------------------------------------------

constraints

-- Ordinary domain invariants, deliberately UNRELATED to the aggregation/
-- composition toggles above, so they stay satisfied identically across
-- both the default and the "off" run: the only thing that should ever
-- differ between the two config files is whether the forced cyclic /
-- forced doubly-owned structures are admitted at all.

context f:Folder inv nameNotEmpty:
  f.name <> ''

context fi:File inv sizePositive:
  fi.size > 0

context a:Archive inv nameNotEmpty:
  a.name <> ''

-- Explicit, directly OCL-checkable statement of the length-1 case of
-- aggregation-cycle-freeness ("a folder is not its own primary parent").
-- Kept as a real invariant (independent of both the plugin's structural
-- search constraint and the 2-hop cross-association cycle test above) so a
-- later SOIL script can satisfy/violate it on its own.
context f:Folder inv notOwnPrimaryParent:
  f.primaryParent <> f
